  "_what_this_is": [
    "Query parameters that identify one click, one campaign or one visitor.",
    "",
    "Two readers, one list. URL canonicalisation strips them, so a tagged URL",
    "is the same page as the clean one. `url.tracking-parameter` reports internal",
    "links that carry one: a value meant for a single visitor's arrival, served",
    "to everyone who reads the page.",
    "",
    "Hand-curated. Each entry cites the operator's own documentation. A parameter",
    "with only third-party evidence (Mailchimp's mc_cid / mc_eid, X's twclid,",
    "Instagram's igshid, at the time of writing) stays out until its operator",
    "documents it.",
    "",
    "`match` is `exact` for a parameter name, or `prefix` for a family such as",
    "utm_*. Names are compared lowercase."
  ],

  "parameters": [
